Proof. Considering (a), let D be a dominating set inGα,β, and letD1 = D\ [x∆, ∆] and
D2 =D\D1. Suppose|D2|<|[x∆, ∆]\D1|. Since∀v∈D2,u∈[x∆, ∆]\D1 wehave degα,β(v)<
degα,β(u), this implies vol(D2) < vol([x∆, ∆] \D1) and thus vol(D) < vol([x∆, ∆]) <⌊eα⌋, a
contradiction.
Suppose in case (b) thatvol([x∆, ∆]) <|[1,x ∆ −1]|and thatD,D 1,D 2 are the same as
in the proof of (a). Again we obtain vol(D2) < vol([x∆, ∆] \D1), which implies vol(D) <
vol([x∆, ∆]) <|[1,x ∆ −1]. Thus the volume of D is not suﬃcient to dominate the subset
[1,x ∆ −1], a contradiction.
