The paper’s native problem is minimum dominating set on exact \((\alpha,\beta)\)-power-law degree sequences. The prior “attach every vertex to a planted dominator” idea does give a valid dominating-set witness, but by itself it says nothing about minimality and leaves an obvious planting signature; I’m now checking whether the paper’s reduction supplies a scalable optimum/approximation certificate or only a worst-case hardness embedding.
